<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bibliotheca Palatina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bibliotheca Palatina was the library of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> palatine at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a>, housed in the Church of the Holy Spirit, and in the sixteenth century one of the finest collections of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> and books in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> troops took Heidelberg in 1622 during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, Maximilian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> presented it to Pope Gregory XV, and it was moved to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vatican-library">Vatican Library</a> in 1623. Some 850 German manuscripts were returned to Heidelberg in 1816.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bibliotheca-palatina.jpg" alt="Bibliotheca Palatina" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Meister des Codex Manesse · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Altstetten.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
